  "utterances": [
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 0.4,
      "end": 2.43,
      "text": "Glimmerdale Homes, this is Ines."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 3.48,
      "end": 6.77,
      "text": "Hi Ines, Sam from Vantrellis. Okay, let's get started."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 7.62,
      "end": 7.98,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 8.62,
      "end": 22.28,
      "text": "I was hoping to use our thirty minutes to understand how crew scheduling works for you today, share what similar teams do, and then decide together if a next step makes sense. Anything you'd add to that?"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 23.03,
      "end": 26.31,
      "text": "No, that works. Leave some time for pricing."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 27.39,
      "end": 31.41,
      "text": "Walk me through what building the crew schedule looks like today?"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 32.49,
      "end": 38.69,
      "text": "Honestly it's a spreadsheet. Our office manager spends about six hours every week on it."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 39.22,
      "end": 41.4,
      "text": "What makes that the hardest part?"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 42.22,
      "end": 49.25,
      "text": "Things change after it's done. Last time, we sent two crews to the same job last month."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 49.61,
      "end": 54.0,
      "text": "And when that happens, what does it look like for you personally?"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 54.82,
      "end": 61.02,
      "text": "I'm the one on the phone apologizing. It's the part of the job I hate."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 61.95,
      "end": 66.72,
      "text": "If nothing changes over the next six months, what does that cost you?"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 67.41,
      "end": 73.61,
      "text": "Honestly? Around eighteen thousand dollars in overtime last quarter. And people are tired of it."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 74.18,
      "end": 75.61,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 76.58,
      "end": 76.95,
      "text": "Yeah."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 77.72,
      "end": 120.63,
      "text": "So let me walk you through the platform. There's the scheduling board, which has drag and drop, color coding, and templates. Then there's the mobile app, which works on iPhone and Android, with push alerts and offline mode. We also have reporting, with twelve standard reports and a custom report builder, and we integrate with payroll, accounting, and most CRMs. There's an admin console for permissions, single sign-on, audit logs, and we have a customer success team that does onboarding. We also just launched route optimization and a customer portal, and there's an API if your team wants to build anything custom. Most customers start with the scheduling board and then add modules as they grow."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 121.25,
      "end": 124.12,
      "text": "Okay. What does something like that cost?"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 124.61,
      "end": 126.78,
      "text": "It's eighteen thousand dollars a year."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 128.13,
      "end": 129.75,
      "text": "That's steep for us."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 130.54,
      "end": 135.3,
      "text": "I hear you. I could probably do fifteen percent off if that helps."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 136.07,
      "end": 138.94,
      "text": "Maybe. I'd have to think about it."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 139.85,
      "end": 143.5,
      "text": "Are you the one who makes the call on this?"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 144.38,
      "end": 146.0,
      "text": "Me and Casey, mostly."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 146.99,
      "end": 151.01,
      "text": "Does what you've seen so far make sense for your team?"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 151.69,
      "end": 156.64,
      "text": "Can you just send me some info and I'll look it over?"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 157.76,
      "end": 163.64,
      "text": "Happy to. So I send the right thing, what would you need to see in it?"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 164.0,
      "end": 169.78,
      "text": "Probably proof it works with our current tools, and something I can show Casey."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 170.53,
      "end": 172.33,
      "text": "Let's reconnect sometime next week."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 173.04,
      "end": 174.24,
      "text": "Sure, sounds good."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_1",
      "role": "REP",
      "start": 175.17,
      "end": 177.35,
      "text": "Thanks Ines, really appreciate the time."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "spk_2",
      "role": "PROSPECT",
      "start": 178.35,
      "end": 179.13,
      "text": "Thanks, bye."
    }
  ],
